<h1>Fan-out to multiple destinations</h1>
<p>In real-world data architectures, you often need to send the same event stream to multiple destination systems — a data warehouse for analytics, a search index for product search, a real-time API for notifications, and so on. This recipe shows how to fan out a single pipeline's output across several destinations.</p>

<h2>The pattern</h2>
<p>Each Godzilla pipeline has one source and one destination. To fan out to multiple destinations, create one pipeline per destination, all reading from the same source connector:</p>

<div class='code-block'>
  <div class='code-block__header'>
    <span class='code-block__filename'>fanout-pattern.txt</span>
    <span class='code-block__lang'>text</span>
    <button class='code-block__copy' type='button'>Copy</button>
  </div>
  <pre class='code-block__pre'><code class='code-block__code'>Source (Kafka topic)
